---
title: "One sticky note: typing, saving, outside edits, archive and Trash"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: editing
    lg1: syncing
    lg2: stored
    lg3: Breaks NoSpuriousConflictBlock in some cases
    lg4: Path to the NoSpuriousConflictBlock bug
    state "Terms" as terms {
      direction TB
      state " " as tc0 {
        direction LR
        tm0: person = The owner, using Sticky Notes on this Mac.
        tm1: save timer = The half-second pause after typing before the note is written to its file.
        tm2: file watcher = The part of the app that notices the note's file changed on disk.
        tm3: outside edit = A change to the note's file made by Obsidian, the other Mac or iCloud.
      }
      state " " as tc1 {
        direction LR
        tm4: conflict version = A second copy of the file that iCloud keeps when two saves disagree.
        tm5: conflict sweep = The app step that merges conflict versions back into the file and appends a 'Conflicted copy' section.
        tm6: other Mac = The owner's second Mac, running Sticky Notes on the same vault.
        tm7: Obsidian = The notes app that shares the vault folder.
      }
      state " " as tc2 {
        direction LR
        tm8: iCloud = iCloud Drive, which syncs the vault between the Macs.
        tm9: archive = Closed notes, still listed in the notes panel.
        tm10: Trash = Notes deleted from the archive, kept 30 days.
      }
    }
  }
  class lg0 blue
  class lg1 orange
  class lg2 teal
  class lg3 mayBreak
  class lg4 bugPath
  s0: File changed, window not told yet
  s1: App quit, note on disk
  s2: Note file deleted
  s3: Typing, save pending
  s4: Note open, nothing pending
  s5: Note in the archive
  s6: Save pending, person in another window
  s7: Typing, save pending, caret out of the text
  s8: Outside edit held back
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: the person quits the app
  s0 --> s2: the person leaves an empty note by closing it or switching away
  s0 --> s3: the person types in the note
  s0 --> s4: the file watcher reports the change [the window shows it]
  s2 --> s1: the person quits the app
  s3 --> s1: the person quits the app
  s3 --> s5: the person clicks the note's close button [the note has text]
  s3 --> s0: the half-second save timer writes the note
  s3 --> s6: the person switches to another window
  s3 --> s7: the person grabs the note's title bar
  s3 --> s8: the file watcher reports the change [the window holds it back]
  s4 --> s1: the person quits the app
  s4 --> s2: the person leaves an empty note by closing it or switching away
  s4 --> s3: the person types in the note
  s5 --> s1: the person quits the app
  s0 --> s5: the person clicks the note's close button [the note has text]
  s6 --> s3: the person clicks into the text
  s6 --> s1: the person quits the app
  s6 --> s5: the person clicks the note's close button [the note has text]
  s6 --> s0: the half-second save timer writes the note
  s6 --> s8: the file watcher reports the change [the window holds it back]
  s7 --> s3: the person clicks into the text
  s7 --> s1: the person quits the app
  s7 --> s5: the person clicks the note's close button [the note has text]
  s7 --> s6: the person switches to another window
  s7 --> s0: the half-second save timer writes the note
  s7 --> s8: the file watcher reports the change [the window holds it back]
  s8 --> s1: the person quits the app
  s8 --> s5: the person clicks the note's close button [the note has text]
  s8 --> s0: the half-second save timer writes the note
  s8 --> s6: the person switches to another window
  s4 --> s5: the person clicks the note's close button [the note has text]
